From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicolai Buchwitz <nb@tipi-net.de>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 20:59:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: bcmgenet: collapse TX priority queues to a single queue

The strict-priority TX queues can starve under multi-queue load and
trip NETDEV WATCHDOG. The multi-queue design was originally used for
STB use cases that are no longer needed (confirmed by Justin Chen at
Broadcom). GENET v1 already exercises a single-queue path. Point v2-v4
at the same configuration: ring 0 takes the full BD pool.

GENET v5 shares the v4 table, so Raspberry Pi 4 / CM4 (BCM2711) is
covered.

Posted to net-next (reviewed by Justin Chen and Florian Fainelli):
https://lore.kernel.org/netdev/20260612205915.3156127-2-nb@tipi-net.de/

Fixes: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/issues/20570

Signed-off-by: Nicolai Buchwitz <nb@tipi-net.de>
Signed-off-by: Stuart Johnson <stuart@stu.org.uk>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/broadcom/genet/bcmgenet.c | 12 ++++++------
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/broadcom/genet/bcmgenet.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/broadcom/genet/bcmgenet.c
@@ -3703,8 +3703,8 @@
 };
 
 static const struct bcmgenet_hw_params bcmgenet_hw_params_v2 = {
-	.tx_queues = 4,
-	.tx_bds_per_q = 32,
+	.tx_queues = 0,
+	.tx_bds_per_q = 0,
 	.rx_queues = 0,
 	.rx_bds_per_q = 0,
 	.bp_in_en_shift = 16,
@@ -3721,8 +3721,8 @@
 };
 
 static const struct bcmgenet_hw_params bcmgenet_hw_params_v3 = {
-	.tx_queues = 4,
-	.tx_bds_per_q = 32,
+	.tx_queues = 0,
+	.tx_bds_per_q = 0,
 	.rx_queues = 0,
 	.rx_bds_per_q = 0,
 	.bp_in_en_shift = 17,
@@ -3739,8 +3739,8 @@
 };
 
 static const struct bcmgenet_hw_params bcmgenet_hw_params_v4 = {
-	.tx_queues = 4,
-	.tx_bds_per_q = 32,
+	.tx_queues = 0,
+	.tx_bds_per_q = 0,
 	.rx_queues = 0,
 	.rx_bds_per_q = 0,
 	.bp_in_en_shift = 17,
